{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "שם האחד גרשום", :translit "shem ha-echad gershom", :gloss "the name of the one was Gershom"} {:he "כי אמר גר וגו'", :translit "ki amar ger vegomer", :gloss "for he said: a stranger etc."} {:he "ושם האחד אליעזר", :translit "veshem ha-echad eliezer", :gloss "and the name of the one was Eliezer"} {:he "כי אלהי אבי בעזרי וגו'", :translit "ki elohai avai be-ezri vegomer", :gloss "for the God of my father was my help etc."} {:he "כי אמר", :translit "ki amar", :gloss "for he said"} {:he "כי אמר", :translit "ki amar", :gloss "for he said"} {:he "כי אמר", :translit "ki amar", :gloss "for he said"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Contrast between presence and absence of כי אמר for each son's name"} {:kind :other, :note "Identification of uncircumcised child at the inn as Eliezer rather than Gershom based on absence of later sons born to Moses in Egypt"}], :frame {:text "The Talmud records that Moses delayed circumcising his son because he reasoned it was dangerous to travel immediately after the procedure; an angel then confronted him on the road. Nedarim 31b-32a discusses Moses's justification. The Talmud in Nedarim 32a identifies the son who was endangered as Gershom. Exodus Rabbah 5:8 discusses the episode of Zipporah circumcising her son at the inn (Exodus 4:24-26). Judges 18:30 records that Jonathan son of Gershom son of Moses became priest for Micah's idol. Ba'al HaTurim cites a midrashic tradition that Jethro stipulated the firstborn son be given to idolatry, which he links to the eventual emergence of Jonathan. The name Eliezer commemorates Moses being saved from Pharaoh after killing the Egyptian (Exodus 2:14-15).", :sources ["Nedarim 31b-32a" "Nedarim 32a" "Exodus Rabbah 5:8" "Exodus 4:24-26" "Judges 18:30" "Exodus 2:14-15"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Contrast between presence and absence of כי אמר for each son's name", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :other, :note "Identification of uncircumcised child at the inn as Eliezer rather than Gershom based on absence of later sons born to Moses in Egypt", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:17:03.811896086Z", :model "glm-5.2"}